---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import BuyButtons from '../components/BuyButtons.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="For families and schools" description="Free Ojadili activity pages, reading the book together, and orders for schools, libraries and community groups.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>For families and schools</h1>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="prose">
          <h2>Reading it together</h2>
          <p>
            I wrote Ojadili for Igbo kids aged 8 to 12 growing up outside Nigeria, and for the parents and
            grandparents who want to pass the old stories on. You don’t need to speak Igbo to follow
            it, and there’s a list of the Igbo words and what they mean on <a href="/story#words">the story page</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            It reads best out loud. Do the <i lang="ig">Ifo chakpii!</i> call at the start and let your
            kids shout back <i lang="ig">Wọo!</i> Afterwards, ask them who they think was right in the
            last fight, and which of his promises Ojadili broke as a boy. Kids tend to have strong
            opinions on both.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you know a version of the Ojadili story from your own family, tell them that one too.
          </p>
        </div>

        <aside class="download">
          <h2>Free activity pages</h2>
          <p>
            The two activity pages from the back of the book: match the Igbo words, guess who said it,
            count the villages and rivers, remember Ojadili’s three promises, and draw your own chi.
            The last one asks kids to say <i lang="ig">Ifo chakpii!</i> to an elder and see if they get a story.
          </p>
          <a class="btn btn--solid" href="/downloads/ojadili-activity-pages.pdf" download>Download the activity pages (PDF)</a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section orders">
    <div class="wrap grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Schools, libraries and community groups</h2>
        <p>
          I can supply copies directly for schools, libraries, Igbo community groups, Saturday
          schools and cultural events, and I’m happy to talk about bulk pricing.
        </p>
        <p>
          Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}?subject=Ojadili%20order`}>{SITE.email}</a> with how
          many copies you need and where you are.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Buying one copy</h2>
        <p>The paperback is on Amazon.</p>
        <BuyButtons />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 0.8fr);
  }
  .grid:has(> :only-child) { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .grid h2 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.4vw, 2.6rem); }
  .download {
    align-self: start;
    background: var(--night);
    color: var(--nzu);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 2rem;
  }
  .download .btn--solid { background: var(--palm); border-color: var(--palm); color: var(--night); }
  .download .btn--solid:hover { background: transparent; color: var(--palm); }
  .orders { background: var(--nzu); padding-top: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6rem) !important; }
  .orders .grid { margin-top: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
